Story 1: GitHub Branch Protection Rules

Enable branch protection on main/master requiring at least one mandatory reviewer approval before any PR can be merged.
Configure the repository to accept only signed commits, ensuring commit authenticity and traceability.
Disable direct pushes to protected branches so all changes must go through a reviewed Pull Request.

Story 2: Automated PR Validation Pipeline

Configure the CI pipeline to trigger automatically whenever a Pull Request is opened or updated against protected branches.
Add a pipeline stage to run linting and terraform validate/terraform fmt to catch syntax errors and formatting issues early.
Integrate a security scanning tool (tfsec or Checkov) into the pipeline to detect misconfigurations before merge.

Story 3: Standardize CI Across Repos

Build a single reusable CI workflow template covering linting, validation, and security scanning stages.
Roll out and apply this standardized template across all organization repositories to eliminate configuration drift.

Story 4: Enforce Status Checks on Merge

Mark CI pipeline results (lint, validate, security scan) as required status checks in branch protection settings.
Configure GitHub to block merging any PR into protected branches until all required checks pass successfully.
